      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Elias is right, because the weight of his story is real, and you should write it with that honesty. He doesn't need a fake happy ending; he needs a story that feels true to the crushing reality of his situation. This is the moment where the character stops trying to fix the world and starts trying to survive it, which is exactly what makes the narrative so painful and necessary.",
